{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## CORRECTION to my earlier comment: I stated the BuildKit storage mechanism WRONG\n\nMy previous comment on this ticket asserted that `docker_unaccounted_bytes` under-reports because\n\"BuildKit build cache is stored under /var/lib/docker/buildkit, NOT under overlay2\". I took that\nfrom the reviewer's finding and repeated it without verifying it. **It is not accurate**, and the\ninaccuracy pointed at a fix that would have been actively harmful.\n\nVerified against moby source: in the classic graphdriver setup,\n`builder/builder-next/controller.go`'s `newGraphDriverController` hands the LIVE `GraphDriver`\nand `LayerStore` to `snapshot.NewSnapshotter`, and every snapshot operation delegates\n(`Prepare` -> `GraphDriver.Create`, `Usage` -> `GraphDriver.DiffSize`). **BuildKit's cache\nsnapshots ARE inside overlay2.** `.../buildkit/` holds metadata DBs plus a content store, not the\ncache snapshots themselves.\n\n## Why the correction changes the fix\n\nMy earlier comment offered two directions: widen the `du` to include buildkit, or narrow the\nledger to Images + Containers. **Narrowing the ledger would have been actively wrong.** Since the\nbuild cache genuinely lives in overlay2, removing its ledger row republishes a fully PRUNABLE\ncache as \"bytes prune cannot reach\", and the alarm then pages on every build against a 2 GiB\nthreshold. That converts a correctness defect into a noisy false-positive pager, which is worse.\n\nWidening the `du` to overlay2 + buildkit was also rejected, for a reason I had not considered: it\npatches a symptom with a hardcoded directory list, and it still breaks under the **containerd\nsnapshotter**, where layers move to `.../containerd/` and `overlay2` goes stale — pegging the\nresidue at its clamp forever on a filling box, i.e. reading healthy precisely when it is not.\n\n## What was actually implemented\n\nBoth sides widened to the same LAYOUT-INDEPENDENT set: `du -sx` of the WHOLE Docker root against\nALL FOUR ledger rows (Local Volumes included). This also captures consumers no ledger row covers\nat all — container JSON logs under `.../containers/<id>/`, BuildKit's content store, and\n`.../image/` metadata.\n\nHonest residual, documented in-tree: a Docker root split across mounts under-reports, because\n`-x` stops at the filesystem boundary. That LOSES SENSITIVITY rather than inventing a page, which\nis the right direction for a residue metric to fail.\n\nAlarm renamed `rebar-docker-unaccounted-overlay2` -> `rebar-docker-unaccounted-bytes` to match.\n\n## The lesson worth keeping\n\nThe reviewer was RIGHT that the arithmetic was broken and WRONG about the mechanism. I relayed the\nmechanism without checking it, and had the implementing agent trusted my restatement it would have\ntaken the narrowing option and shipped a worse metric than the one it replaced. A blocking review\nfinding identifies a defect; its explanation is a hypothesis and needs verifying like any other."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788551640298113001,"uuid":"c903d63f-48c4-4fdf-b047-200f5d7efed6"}